  "description": "Alterations to the main entrance,&nbsp; the public realm in front of the adjacent facade bays and gate to the rear of 18-22 Shacklewell Lane.&nbsp;",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;By virtue of removing publically accessible cycle parking the proposal would fail to promote sustainable modes of transport, contrary to&amp;nbsp; London Plan Policies T1,T6 and Local Plan Policies P33 Policies LP42, LP45 and TR4 of the NPPF&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of its scale, appearance and location would result in an obstructive and intrusive form of development that would obstruct the pavement, reduce the amount of space available for use by pedestrians, block lines of sight creating blind spots and create distractions for highway users reducing the safety of the highway. As such the proposed development is contrary to policy D8 &#x27;Public Realm&#x27; of the London Plan (2021) as well as policy PP1 &#x27;Public Realm&#x27;, LP7 &#x27;Advertisements&#x27; and LP42 &#x27;Walking and Cycling&#x27; of the Hackney Local Plan and TR4 of the NPPF 2026.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
